  "subject": "Session closeout 2026-08-24: seat resumed after a ~10-week gap; an unbriefed adopter-org field report triaged into four merged implementer fixes; skill suite redesigned 7->6 cards with a two-axis naming rule; and the session's main output -- the Director-originated split of COMMUNICATION SUBSTRATE (durable, ratified, seat-addressable, auditable, enumerable; memos/ by default, Jira permitted) from DOORBELL TRANSPORT (ephemeral, swappable), governed by one rule: a notification MUST NOT be the transport, it carries a pointer into the substrate -- which supplies the architectural rationale for pointer-not-payload that the June decision had justified only on prompt-injection grounds. Also: channels adapter retired as a reference transport; .orgdef seat addressing adopted (<seat>@<charter-id>.orgdef, conferred by claim-seat, git authorship unified on it); the implementer-returned finding 'a seat cannot know it is deaf' accepted and escalated to a defect in the RATIFIED doorbell decision with four attestation requirements; and conformance #3 ruled transport-independence-met but promotion HELD on the one leg where no live seat has yet been woken by the vendor-neutral transport. Two commits merged (65e73d7, 3b5dd47); two proposals and seven memos drafted awaiting Director ratification.",

