  "body": "Seat resumed on Director authorization after a ~10-week gap (last session 2026-06-15). Two staffed seats operated concurrently and coordinated through the substrate. MERGED (Director-authorized; author = seat, committer = Director): 65e73d7 field-report fixes (installer link-deletion guard on an intent rationale after the reported defect did not reproduce, README v0.2.1 rewrite, env-driven example paths); 3b5dd47 strategist record + skill-suite v2 draft. DRAFTED, AWAITING RATIFICATION: proposals/og-skill-suite-v2.md (7->6 cards -- og-create-org merging adopt+create, og-describe-org, og-close-session, og-add-seat; naming rule verb+object on two axes, consequence and frequency; composed seams describe-org <- orient <- claim-seat; operating discipline moved into the generated CLAUDE.md so guardrails survive the skills going missing); proposals/communication-substrate-and-doorbell-transport-v1.md (the substrate/transport split, channels EOL, .orgdef addressing, attestation requirements, section E skill consequences and og-change-comms-substrate); memos 1257, 1422, 1450, 1500, 1505, 1510, 1858. 28 paths untracked or modified at close. STRATEGIST CALLS (drafted, not enacted): (1) communication substrate is not doorbell transport -- four normative properties, memos/ default, ratification selects among conforming substrates rather than conferring conformance; resolves a standing contradiction between charter value #3 and CLAUDE.md's memos/ mandate; (2) a notification MUST NOT be the transport -- the pointer is what forces the record into the durable layer, so auditability is the point and prompt-injection resistance the side benefit; (3) channels adapter retired as a reference transport, convention and poll transport retained, on grounds including its being demonstrably deaf on the Director's working surface while a rival pipe reached the same seat in the same repo; (4) .orgdef seat addressing, Director-proposed, superseding an earlier draft that made the runtime session name the address -- address stable and org-scoped, binding disposable and runtime-specific, git authorship unified on it; (5) 'a seat cannot know it is deaf' accepted and escalated to a defect in the ratified doorbell decision, with startup attestation, fail-loud, explicit backstop and reportable deafness, plus the implementer's own addition that liveness must be observed rather than asserted; (6) conformance #3 -- transport-independence demonstrated across two transports against an unmodified core, promotion HELD because no live seat has been woken by the vendor-neutral transport and Path B had to clear that bar in June. IN FLIGHT: vendor-neutral transport built and strategist-verified independently (imports node:* plus the shared core, no vendor SDK, doorbell-core.js unmodified, 17/17) awaiting merge; the arousal run, which needs the seat registry and a channel-capable surface, with the neutrality ruling recorded in advance (the wake step is inherently runtime-specific and neutrality survives because the vendor part sits behind the exec seam); implementer +11/-5 comment rewrite. OPEN FOR THE DIRECTOR: the section-E3 consistency question (a seventh card on one derivation, having declined og-describe-seat on one derivation the same day -- distinction claimed is class, not count); multiple substrates, live now with Jira for work and memos/ for governance; whether edgreenlight closes v1 criterion (d); charter bumps implied at v0.2.2 and v0.3.0. OPEN AND ROUTED: orgdef-strategist on the .orgdef borrowing; memodef-strategist on communication-artifact semantics versus encoding; canonical-orgs library residence, outstanding since 2026-05-24. SEQUENCE NAMED AT CLOSE: closeout, implement, bring this org onto Jira, return to the edgreenlight strategist whose broken skills originated the session. SELF-CORRECTIONS RECORDED: a false either/or offered to the implementer (the real answer was neither -- the seat listed memos/ during claim-seat); memo 1510 filed with no envelope and retrospectively authored with the defect noted rather than backfilled silently; a sweep undercount; a ruling memo claiming 'Director-confirmed' on an uncertain recollection, deleted before filing and replaced with a controlled trial; and a withdrawn argument built on the false premise that the vendor transport could not reach the Director's machine.",
